<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gonaïves</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gonaïves is a port city on the west coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haiti">Haiti</a>, the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/artibonite">Artibonite</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a>. On 1 January 1804 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jean-jacques-dessalines">Jean-Jacques Dessalines</a> proclaimed the independence of Haiti there, and it is known as the City of Independence. It has often been the starting point of Haitian uprisings, including the revolts against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jean-claude-duvalier">Jean-Claude Duvalier</a> in 1985 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jean-bertrand-aristide">Jean-Bertrand Aristide</a> in 2004, and it was devastated by floods in 2004 and 2008.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gonaives.jpg" alt="Gonaïves" width="320" height="179" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fernandolouverture · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cathedral_of_the_Souvenir_Gonaives.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
